      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-17T08:04:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i\u0027m wondering if the boot issues you see are related to\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3139975\n\nit\u0027s pretty common for us to not have a USB DB plugged in on early boards,\nso i\u0027m a bit surprised at the amount of special case code needed here.",
      "revId": "65f8612b5bb389b699fdf5be4d6cc9fa5e54d913",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a35b3d2d_d58bd131",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1477218
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-17T13:48:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the original problem is blocked by i2c storm of PS8815, and it\u0027s difficult to power on without DB even if we trigger powerbtn event.\n\nAfter merged CL-3139975, in most condition, it can power on without DB when plug in AC. But, it still has failure rate system cannot \"auto\" power on without DB.\nFrom log (I upload to comment#12 of b:197585292), it\u0027s late to acquire MB(USBC0) power source before PB task is timeout. System still can be turn on by trigger powerbtn this moment.\n\nI suspect it could be caused by task scheduling, but I\u0027m not familiar task scheduling. Could I have your advise?\n\nIf this condition is not problem, I\u0027ll remove DB detect policy and update patch later.",
      "parentUuid": "5de868e9_993dda21",
      "revId": "65f8612b5bb389b699fdf5be4d6cc9fa5e54d913",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "241366f7_651e76c3",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-17T23:21:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "on very early brya, i saw some issues with the PB task timing out due to\nthe battery waking up slowly. we did not submit this change because it\nshouldn\u0027t be necessary.\n\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/2766485",
      "parentUuid": "a35b3d2d_d58bd131",
      "revId": "65f8612b5bb389b699fdf5be4d6cc9fa5e54d913",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
