      "writtenOn": "2021-09-17T23:21:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ya, this is not a good use of CONFIG_SYSTEM_UNLOCKED.\nboard_id() is a better check. it\u0027s really the board\nrevision, so it should increment with each board spin\nor build phase.\n\npersonally, i would not define CONFIG_SYSTEM_UNLOCKED\n(or remove it right after initial bringup/power-on)\nbecause the system\u0027s locked state is determined by whether\nprogrammables are write-protected, etc. even when\nCONFIG_SYSTEM_UNLOCKED is not defined.",
      "parentUuid": "2c00c813_8fa3887f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 74,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 74,
        "endChar": 30
